@Waypoint.Api_HostAddress = http://localhost:5205

### Health — unauthenticated liveness/version probe (see backend/README.md "Container
### health"). This is what nginx and an operator's monitoring hit first.
GET {{Waypoint.Api_HostAddress}}/api/v1/health
Accept: application/json

### Login — dev-grade local auth (ADR-0004 rollout note). Fails closed until
### LocalAuth__AdminPasswordHash is set on the running process; see backend/README.md
### "Run locally" for how to compute the hash. Named `login` so later requests can pull
### the session token out of its response body.
# @name login
POST {{Waypoint.Api_HostAddress}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "username": "admin",
  "password": "<your-dev-password>"
}

### Current user — Viewer role or higher; exercises the LocalSession bearer token.
GET {{Waypoint.Api_HostAddress}}/api/v1/auth/me
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.token}}

### Catalog — paginated list, Viewer role or higher — demonstrates the X-Total-Count
### convention (docs/api-contract.md Conventions: "Pagination").
GET {{Waypoint.Api_HostAddress}}/api/v1/catalog/artifacts?limit=1&offset=0
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.token}}

### Catalog sync — Admin-only — demonstrates 403 (documented error envelope) for an
### authenticated principal below the required role. Log in as a non-Admin session to
### see it fail; the in-memory local-auth service only issues Admin sessions today.
POST {{Waypoint.Api_HostAddress}}/api/v1/catalog/sync
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.token}}
